Key competitive takeaway

The strongest point emerging from the comparison is that the integrated four-year structure itself is highly differentiated online. Most online competitors offer either Computer Science with a data/AI major or a standalone Data Science/Data Analytics bachelor. They generally do not provide both a Bachelor of Computer Science and a Master of Data Science within four years.

There is one particularly important structural competitor outside the online market: The University of Queensland offers a Bachelor of Computer Science/Master of Data Science in four years, but the program is delivered at St Lucia rather than online. Its 2026 domestic entry threshold was ATAR 97, with Mathematical Methods required.

So from a product-marketing perspective, the clearest whitespace is:

“Two qualifications — Bachelor of Computer Science + Master of Data Science — in four years, delivered online.”

That is much more distinctive than simply positioning around AI, data science or industry relevance, which nearly all five competitors already use.
